# Windows-side bridge scripts are byte artifacts: they are deployed to
%LOCALAPPDATA%\opencode-psmux-bridge and must stay byte-identical to the
# installed copy, or the repo stops being a faithful mirror of what runs.
#
# Without this, git will normalise CRLF to LF on commit on some machines and
# the next deploy will not match the tracked bytes. Observed exactly that
# drift in scripts/windows/bin/psmux.cmd before this file existed.
#
# -text: never convert line endings, in either direction.
# binary is deliberately NOT used, so git diff still produces a usable
# line-oriented diff for a text file.
scripts/windows/** -text
